<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Project Title:</strong> IMovies — Movie Ticket Booking Made Simple</li>
  <li><strong>Domain:</strong> Full Stack Web Engineering / Online Entertainment &amp; Ticketing</li>
  <li><strong>Technology Stack:</strong> MERN (MongoDB, Express.js, React.js 19, Node.js)</li>
  <li><strong>Team Members:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lead Developer:</strong> Full Stack MERN Developer</li>
      <li><strong>Roles &amp; Responsibilities:</strong> System Architecture, Frontend UI/UX Engineering, Backend REST API Development, MongoDB Database Modeling, Atomic Concurrency Control, and Quality Assurance.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Project Overview</h2>
<h3>2.1 Purpose</h3>
<p><strong>IMovies</strong> is a modern, responsive web application engineered to streamline the cinema discovery and ticket booking experience. Built from the ground up using the MERN stack, it eliminates conventional reservation bottlenecks through an interactive seating matrix, time-sensitive availability tracking, dynamic price calculation, and real-time double-booking prevention.</p>

<h3>2.2 Key Features &amp; Capabilities</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Comprehensive Movie Showcase:</strong> Real-time listing of 8 curated blockbuster titles featuring high-resolution poster art, genres, durations, age ratings, synopsis, and director/cast listings.</li>
  <li><strong>Instant Title Search &amp; Multi-Attribute Filtering:</strong> Dynamic search input combined with genre and language dropdown selectors.</li>
  <li><strong>Cinema Theatres &amp; Showtime Scheduling:</strong> Multi-cinema listings spanning Bangalore, Chennai, and Hyderabad across various dates.</li>
  <li><strong>Real-Time Showtime Expiration Logic:</strong> Automatically compares showtime hours against the current system time; marks elapsed shows as <code>Expired / Booking Closed</code> to prevent invalid bookings.</li>
  <li><strong>Interactive Seating Layout:</strong> Visually displays theater screen orientation and individual seats across multiple rows, dynamically highlighting <em>Available</em>, <em>Selected</em>, and <em>Booked</em> states.</li>
  <li><strong>Atomic Double-Booking Prevention:</strong> Utilizes MongoDB atomic operators (<code>$addToSet</code> with <code>$not $elemMatch</code>) to guarantee zero overlapping seat reservations during concurrent checkout attempts.</li>
  <li><strong>JWT Authentication &amp; Password Encryption:</strong> Stateless JSON Web Token authentication with 12-round bcrypt password hashing.</li>
  <li><strong>Booking Summary &amp; Confirmation:</strong> Generates unique booking reference IDs (e.g., <code>IMOV-JURX6PW9</code>) and a complete itemized ticket breakdown.</li>
  <li><strong>User Reservation History &amp; Instant Cancellation:</strong> Users can view all previous bookings and cancel reservations, immediately returning seats to the available pool.</li>
  <li><strong>Modern Purple &amp; White Design:</strong> Accessible, high-contrast user interface styled in royal purple (<code>#7c3aed</code>), clean lavender surfaces, and crisp white cards.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Architecture</h2>

<h3>3.1 Frontend Architecture (React.js)</h3>
<p>The client is structured as a Single Page Application (SPA) leveraging modern React 19 and Vite:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Vite Build Tool:</strong> Powers instant Hot Module Replacement (HMR) and optimized minified client bundles.</li>
  <li><strong>Declarative Routing:</strong> <code>react-router-dom</code> (v7) governs client navigation with protected route guards (<code>&lt;PrivateRoute&gt;</code>) restricting unauthenticated access.</li>
  <li><strong>State Management:</strong> Centralized React <code>Context API</code> (<code>AuthContext</code>) manages authentication tokens, user sessions, and login/logout lifecycles. Component-level state governs real-time seat matrices and search inputs.</li>
  <li><strong>HTTP Communication:</strong> An Axios client layer with an interceptor automatically attaches the <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code> header to protected requests.</li>
  <li><strong>Toast Notifications:</strong> <code>react-hot-toast</code> provides non-blocking notifications for booking events, validation errors, and session status.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.2 Backend Architecture (Node.js &amp; Express.js)</h3>
<p>The backend follows the Model-View-Controller (MVC) architectural pattern:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Express REST API:</strong> Modular routers handle distinct resource domains (<code>/api/auth</code>, <code>/api/movies</code>, <code>/api/theatres</code>, <code>/api/shows</code>, <code>/api/bookings</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Middleware Pipeline:</strong> Includes CORS headers, JSON request body parsing, JWT token authentication, and centralized error handling.</li>
  <li><strong>Atomic Seat Reservation Strategy:</strong> The booking controller executes atomic updates via <code>Show.findOneAndUpdate(...)</code> to prevent race conditions without external distributed locks.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.3 Database Architecture (MongoDB &amp; Mongoose)</h3>
<p>MongoDB models define schema constraints, indices, and relationships:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>User:</strong> Stores customer credentials (name, unique email, bcrypt-hashed password with <code>select: false</code>, role).</li>
  <li><strong>Movie:</strong> Stores movie metadata (title, synopsis, genres, languages, duration, rating, poster URL, cast, director).</li>
  <li><strong>Theatre:</strong> Defines cinema venue details (name, location, city, row count, seats per row, total capacity).</li>
  <li><strong>Show:</strong> Maps movies to specific theatres, dates, showtimes, base ticket prices, and an active array of <code>bookedSeats</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Booking:</strong> Permanent transaction ledger recording unique reference code, customer ID, show reference, reserved seat numbers, total price, and status.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Setup Instructions</h2>

<h3>4.1 Prerequisites</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Node.js:</strong> v18.0.0 or higher</li>
  <li><strong>npm:</strong> v9.0.0 or higher</li>
  <li><strong>MongoDB:</strong> Community Server v6.0 or v9.0 running locally on port 27017</li>
  <li><strong>Web Browser:</strong> Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, or Microsoft Edge</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.2 Step-by-Step Installation</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Open Project Directory:</strong>
    <pre>cd IMovies</pre>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Install Backend Dependencies:</strong>
    <pre>cd backend
npm install</pre>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Configure Backend Environment (<code>backend/.env</code>):</strong>
    <pre>PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/imovies
JWT_SECRET=imovies_dev_secret_key_2024_change_in_prod
JWT_EXPIRE=7d
NODE_ENV=development</pre>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Install Frontend Dependencies:</strong>
    <pre>cd ../frontend
npm install</pre>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Seed Sample Data (8 Movies, 4 Theatres, 325 Shows):</strong>
    <pre>cd ../backend
node seed/seedDB.js</pre>
  </li>
</ol>

