<h2>8. Authentication &amp; Authorization</h2>
<p>Authentication is handled through industry-standard cryptographic techniques:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>JWT Tokens:</strong> Generated upon login/register with a 7-day expiration time using HMAC SHA-256 signatures.</li>
  <li><strong>Password Hashing:</strong> Passwords undergo salted one-way hashing using <code>bcryptjs</code> with 12 rounds of salt generation before storage.</li>
  <li><strong>Protected Routes:</strong> Handled on the frontend via <code>&lt;PrivateRoute&gt;</code> and on the backend via Express <code>protect</code> middleware checking the HTTP <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code> header.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. User Interface Design</h2>
<p>The user interface has been styled with an elegant <strong>Purple and White</strong> design system:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Color Palette:</strong> Royal Purple (<code>#7c3aed</code>), Crisp White (<code>#ffffff</code>), Soft Lavender Surfaces (<code>#f3f0fb</code>), and Midnight Violet Typography (<code>#18132b</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Key Screens:</strong>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Home Page:</strong> Hero banner, call-to-action buttons, key benefit cards, and now-showing movie grid.</li>
      <li><strong>Movie Catalog:</strong> Title search bar, dynamic genre/language dropdowns, and responsive movie cards.</li>
      <li><strong>Movie Details:</strong> High-resolution backdrop, movie metadata, and showtime cards with real-time <code>Available</code> and <code>Expired</code> badges.</li>
      <li><strong>Interactive Seat Map:</strong> Curved theater screen indicator, responsive seat buttons with color-coded states, and dynamic live subtotal.</li>
      <li><strong>Confirmation &amp; History:</strong> Ticket summary with unique alphanumeric booking references and an instant cancellation feature.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>10. Testing</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>API Endpoint Testing:</strong> Verified all REST routes using automated HTTP scripts. Ensured status codes <code>200</code>, <code>201</code>, <code>400</code>, <code>401</code>, and <code>409</code> are returned appropriately.</li>
  <li><strong>Double-Booking Race Condition Test:</strong> Dispatched duplicate simultaneous requests for identical seats; confirmed that the second request is consistently rejected with <code>409 Conflict</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Showtime Expiration Validation:</strong> Verified that showtimes preceding the current clock time are marked as expired and cannot be reserved.</li>
  <li><strong>Cancellation Verification:</strong> Confirmed that cancelling a reservation restores the seats to available status.</li>
  <li><strong>Frontend Build Validation:</strong> Built production artifacts via Vite (<code>npm run build</code>) with zero errors across all 97 modules.</li>
</ul>

