<h2>12. Known Issues &amp; Limitations</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Demo Payment:</strong> Payment processing simulates successful checkout for demonstration purposes without real financial gateway integrations.</li>
  <li><strong>External Poster CDN:</strong> Movie posters are fetched from TMDb's CDN; an active internet connection is required for images to load.</li>
  <li><strong>Token Storage:</strong> JWT tokens are stored in browser <code>localStorage</code>; production implementations can switch to <code>httpOnly</code> cookies for enhanced security.</li>
</ul>

<h2>13. Future Enhancements</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Live Payment Gateway:</strong> Integration with Razorpay, Stripe, or PayPal for real financial transactions.</li>
  <li><strong>Digital QR Code Tickets:</strong> Generate scannable QR codes for booking confirmation passes.</li>
  <li><strong>Admin Management Portal:</strong> Dedicated management interface to upload new titles, manage halls, and set dynamic show prices.</li>
  <li><strong>Automated Notifications:</strong> Delivery of ticket receipts and calendar reminders via SMS, Email (SendGrid), or WhatsApp API.</li>
  <li><strong>Snacks &amp; Concessions:</strong> Add-on selection of food and beverages during the seat selection flow.</li>
</ul>

